// Every key that arrived, not one of them.
//
// The backend queues key events in a ring of 256 and drops silently once it is
// full. A frame that consumed one key consumed about thirty a second, because a
// keystroke re-lays the page -- so a held arrow filled the ring in eight
// seconds and everything typed behind it was lost with nothing said. Measured:
// 900 Right presses moved the caret about ninety characters and the text typed
// after them never arrived at all.
//
// The loop stops on -1, which is "the queue is empty", and on a quit, which
// gfx_poll repeats forever once the window has closed -- stopping only on -1
// would spin there.
ed_drain() {
  int k = ed_poll();
  while(k != 0 - 1 && ed_live(k) == 1) {
    k = ed_poll();
  }
} return int k;
